{"id": "1.2-00021", "case_id": "github_lvyufeng_step_mips_lab10_direct_v1", "parent_id": null, "source": "github/lvyufeng/step_into_mips", "record_protocol": null, "panels": {"stored": "<h2>Agent task and scoring</h2><div class='card'><table><tbody><tr><th style='width:175px'>Input task</th><td class='path'>Project specification, interfaces, and permitted public assets</td></tr><tr><th style='width:175px'>Agent context</th><td class='path'>Direct agent workspace: <a href='#task=1.2&amp;case=1.2-00021&amp;file_q=public%2F'>public/</a> (33 files)</td></tr><tr><th style='width:175px'>Expected output</th><td class='path'>Required RTL: src/lab_10_tiny_os/boot_rom.v, src/lab_10_tiny_os/bram_ram.v, src/lab_10_tiny_os/ddr_backend_cdc.v, src/lab_10_tiny_os/ddr_bridge.v, src/lab_10_tiny_os/gpio_mmio.v, src/lab_10_tiny_os/irq_controller.v, src/lab_10_tiny_os/simple_bus.v, src/lab_10_tiny_os/soc.v and 24 more. <a href='#task=1.2&amp;case=1.2-00021&amp;file=public%2Foutput_contract.json'>Open full output contract</a></td></tr><tr><th style='width:175px'>Hidden reference</th><td class='path'>32 RTL files under private/reference/; <a href='#task=1.2&amp;case=1.2-00021&amp;file=private%2Freference%2Fsrc%2Fcommon%2Fuart_rx.v'>open first reference file</a></td></tr><tr><th style='width:175px'>Private score</th><td class='path'>Passed verification testpoints divided by total testpoints, using testbenches or formal verification<br><strong>1 verification testpoints:</strong> lab10. <a href='#task=1.2&amp;case=1.2-00021&amp;file=private%2Fscoring.json'>Open private scoring contract</a></td></tr></tbody></table></div><h2>Case-stored agent instruction</h2><div class='card'><p class='muted'>These are case-stored instructions. A launcher may add framing or execution limits; its saved trajectory is the exact runtime record.</p><details><summary>public/instruction.md · <a href='#task=1.2&amp;case=1.2-00021&amp;file=public%2Finstruction.md'>Open raw</a></summary><pre># MIPS Lab10 StepOS system project\nImplement the final Lab10 SoC, with soc integration top and the complete32-file RTL closure. Read specification/docs/lab_10_tiny_os.md, the Lab10 README and the preceding inherited hardware-contract documents supplied unchanged. This case represents one final integrated system; earlier incremental labs are not additional cases.\n\n- Implement the documented pipelined MIPS subset, forwarding/hazard handling, byte strobes, wait-state data accesses, CP0-like interrupt/eret behavior, UART, GPIO, timer/interrupt controller and DDR bridge/clock crossing. The public declaration-only interfaces retain all selected ports and parameter defaults. $zero is hardwired0. Memory and pipeline control must remain stable while waiting for d_ready; stores commit once. Exceptions use the documented fixed0x180 vector. This teaching ISA has no MMU/TLB, privilege separation or hardware syscall exception; callable software ABI implements its syscall-like services.\n- Preserve the documented byte address map: ROM0..0x3fff, BRAM0x10000..0x1ffff; GPIO/UART/timer/IRQ/DDR-status at0x10000000/0x10001000/0x10002000/0x10003000/0x10004000; DDR window0x80000000..0x87ffffff. The ROM has4096 32-bit words and uses the provided immutable lab_10_boot.mem image. Firmware and DDR behavioral endpoint are inputs/environment support, not RTL the model must invent. A public copy of the image and original software generator is provided; exact firmware must remain unchanged.\n- soc CPU runs on clk and its peripheral simple_bus on bus_clk, with the original half-cycle timing. The external DDR command/response interface may stall and uses its own documented CDC handshake. The scored system connects to the retained upstream ddr_model; physical MIG IP, pin-level DDR2 timing and board clock primitives are outside this portable generation case.\n- Implement the firmware-visible peripheral registers according to the supplied original Lab5-9 documents. Reset follows declared reset ports and clears control/pending state; UART is8N1. The bench reduces clock/baud/timer parameters to accelerate simulation, so honor parameters rather than hardcoding board50MHz/115200baud values.\n- The system must boot the supplied StepOS image, pass DDR calibration/pattern tests, respond to help/ps/mem/led/run demo shell commands, and run its two-task round-robin timer scheduler. Preserve documented software-defined BRAM storage. Native observer paths used to inspect the scheduler/CPU are explicitly listed in specification/native_observers.txt; these are required debug hooks for this historical system harness, not undisclosed grading internals.\n- All usable original benches for the final Lab10 system are retained. Its one complete system bench is one point; commands, UART characters and scheduler observations inside it are not separate cases or points. Earlier lab benches instantiate different hardware versions and are excluded. Board timing and physical deployment claims in README are outside this simulation qualification.\n\nSimulation I/O, delays, force/release, final blocks and external includes are forbidden. Constant elaboration functions ($clog2, $unsigned, $signed, $bits) and synthesizable storage initialization are permitted. Save all RTL under the exact required paths; only those files are collected.\n\nInitialize ROM with the supplied4096 words using synthesizable initial assignments; simulator file-I/O calls are forbidden.\n\nInherited ISA clarification: this teaching pipeline has NO branch delay slot; JAL writes PC+4. The implemented subset is add/sub/and/or/slt, lw/sw/beq/addi/j, lui/ori/andi/xori/bne/jr/jal/addu/subu/sll/srl and the documented CP0 instructions. Subword load/store instructions and other full MIPS32 features listed as future work in the original docs are not required. The final Lab10 address map overrides smaller earlier-lab maps.\n</pre></details></div>"}, "files": [{"name": "case.json", "url": "assets/9e6ea8190a5fba63b6008c3f7c142bf0797ba070e15b63a92f05b6ec3e32